    ── spectral invariants (adjacency of the ring graph; clean bond=1, cross-link=k centers) ──
    spectral radius ρ = 3.4142  (> 2 ⟹ branched: a cross-link lifts the principal mode above the bare ring)
    spectrum (ordered by |λ| descending, so λ₂ here IS the one the gap uses): [+3.414, -3.414, +0.586, -0.586]
    spectral gap (ρ − |λ₂|) = 0.0000 — a wide gap means one mode dominates (the ring leans on a single strut); a gap of 0 is a flat/degenerate top spectrum, NO privileged mode (the symmetric, settled reading, not a deficiency).
    graph energy Σ|λ| = 8.0000 — the ring's total spectral weight; where ρ is stiffness (the dominant mode), this is toughness (the reserve carried across all modes).
